/E (one-way function is a mathematical operation that is easy to compute in one direction, but computationally infeasible to invert given only the output. In asymmetric cryptography, this guarantees that generating a public key from a private value or encrypting a message is fast, while deriving the original secret from the public data would require an impractical amount of time and computing power.)
